; ============================================================
;  ZONE GRID - HOW MANY OF A THING SHARE ONE SQUARE
;
;  WHAT CAN stack is decided in the script, not here. A section marked
;  dont_stack never piles, and neither does anything carrying upgrades.
;  Everything else does: a part-used medkit stacks with its own kind and
;  the number on the square is the total uses left, and wear does not
;  keep two things apart. FOOD AND DRINK are the exception - two of them
;  only share a square when their freshness is within ten percent,
;  because on a tin that bar is how rotten it is.
;
;  What is here is the CEILING. Without one, a stack is unlimited and a
;  grid stops meaning anything - forty bandages in one square is not an
;  inventory, it is a list with extra steps.
;
;  Everything not named below has a ceiling of one: its own square, the
;  way it has been since the grid arrived.
;
;  There is an MCM slider that scales every number here at once, for
;  players who want tighter or looser stacking without editing a file.
;  The result is never less than one.
;
;  FOUR WAYS TO NAME SOMETHING, most specific first:
;
;    [grid_stack_section]   this exact section
;    [grid_stack_like]      any section whose name contains this
;    [grid_stack_flag]      anything whose section carries this key
;    [grid_stack_kind]      anything the game gives this `kind`
;
;  `kind` is the game's own word for what a thing is - the same one the
;  sorting tabs read - so a mod that adds a new bandage gets the
;  bandage ceiling without anybody editing anything.
; ============================================================

[grid_stack_kind]
; Medicine. A first aid kit is a box the size of your palm and you
; carry six; they go in the same pocket.
i_medical           = 5

; Food and drink. Tins and bottles, and the same argument.
i_food              = 5
i_drink             = 5
i_mutant_cooked     = 4
i_mutant_raw        = 4

; Weapon parts, and the upgrade kits that go with them. This is the
; kind that eats a grid alive: you come home from one workshop run with
; thirty of them.
i_part              = 10
i_upgrade           = 5

; Mutant parts, sold by the handful.
i_mutant_part       = 5
i_mutant_belt       = 5

; ------------------------------------------------------------
;  AND THE KINDS THAT WERE MISSING
;
;    "also add other missing Item stacks in incentory like Ammo,
;     scraps etc and you decide what ammount for each should be now"
;
;  Chosen by how many of a thing you actually end a run holding, not by
;  how big it is: the ceiling is what stops a grid turning into a list,
;  and a kind you only ever carry two of does not need one.
; ------------------------------------------------------------

; AMMUNITION, and the biggest of these by a distance. Cartridges arrive
; a box at a time from every corpse on the map, and a full box is one
; square whether it holds five rounds or fifty. Twenty deep is a
; bandolier's worth and still leaves the number meaning something.
;
; `w_ammo` is a w_ kind and stacks anyway - see the note in the audit.
; The w_ prefix is SortingPlus's grouping for "goes with a weapon", not
; a claim that it IS one.
w_ammo              = 20

; Scrap, oddments and everything the game files under nothing in
; particular: bolts, wire, tins, the stuff a workbench eats.
i_misc              = 10

; Dead artefacts. Worth carrying by the handful, worth nothing each.
i_arty_junk         = 10

; Notes, letters and documents. Paper, and weightless with it.
i_letter            = 20

; TOOLS AND KITS, deliberately shallow. These carry a condition, so the
; window only stacks ones within a tenth of each other anyway - and
; four spare screwdrivers in a square is help, forty is a spreadsheet.
i_tool              = 4
i_kit               = 4
i_repair            = 4

; NOT HERE, on purpose:
;   i_quest    a quest item is one thing and wants its own square
;   i_device   detectors and the PDA - few, bulky, and each one is
;              its own state
;   i_arty     a live artefact is never interchangeable with another
;   i_backpack a pack you are not wearing is already an odd thing to
;              be carrying two of

[grid_stack_like]
; ============================================================
;  FACTION PATCHES
;
;  "later players can carry tens of them they super small item that
;   weights nothing so 6 of those should not take the same ammount of
;   space as a assult riffle"
;
;  Quite right. They are cloth badges. The base game gives them no kind
;  of their own - SortingPlus names each one by hand - so they are
;  matched on their name instead, which is how every one of them is
;  built: csky_patch, dolg_patch, freedom_patch, and so on.
; ============================================================
_patch              = 20

; ============================================================
;  BY SECTION FLAG
;
;    "i need that magazines are unstackable in inventory only in the
;     box"
;
;  Some things are best identified by a FLAG in their section rather
;  than by their kind or their name. A magazine is the example: its
;  `kind` is w_ammo, the same as a box of cartridges, so it inherits
;  the ceiling meant for cartridges - and there is no name every
;  magazine in every pack shares. What they do all carry is `is_mag`,
;  which is the flag the magazine mod itself reads.
;
;  Each line is a section key that is either there or not, and the
;  ceiling for anything that has it. This beats the kind and loses to
;  a name pattern or an exact section.
;
;  THIS DOES NOT TOUCH THE MAGAZINE BOX. What stacks inside a box is
;  that box's own amp_box_stack, in mod_system_amp_boxes.ltx, and it
;  still holds ten magazines to a square.
; ============================================================
[grid_stack_flag]
is_mag              = 1

[grid_stack_section]
; ============================================================
;    "make so the "Bolt" item is stackable up to 40."
;
;  Here rather than under a kind, because a bolt is unlike everything
;  that shares its kind: it is the one thing in the Zone you are given
;  an endless supply of and never spend, so you end up carrying a
;  handful you did not ask for. Forty in one square is the number that
;  was asked for and it is the right shape of number - the point is
;  that they stop taking up room you can see.
; ============================================================
bolt                                         = 40
; ============================================================
;  ONE THING AT A TIME
;
;  Anything whose ceiling should not follow its kind goes here, and
;  this list wins over both of the above. The kinds do the work; every
;  line here is a line somebody has to keep up to date, so there had
;  better be a reason for it.
;
;  For example, to let bandages pile deeper than the rest of the
;  medicine:
;
;      bandage = 10
; ============================================================

; ==========================================================
;  EVERY ITEM IN THIS INSTALL, READY TO UNCOMMENT
;
;  1785 of them, grouped by the kind the game gives them and
;  sorted by id inside each group. TAKE THE ; OFF A LINE AND
;  CHANGE THE NUMBER - that is the whole of it.
;
;  Each line is already filled in with its own kind's ceiling
;  from above, so uncommenting one on its own changes nothing.
;  A line here beats the kind and the name rules both.
;
;  Left out on purpose: weapons and outfits, because the
;  window refuses to stack them and a line here would look
;  like a bug; anything the game marks dont_stack, for the
;  same reason.
;
;  NOT EVERYTHING IS HERE. Most of the base game's items live
;  inside Anomaly's packed .db archives, which are not files
;  and cannot be read. A base item is below only if some mod
;  also touches it - which in this install is most of them.
;  Anything missing can still be typed in by hand; it works
;  exactly the same.
; ==========================================================

